# Final Regression Model Comparison

## Evaluation Results

| Evaluation Metric | Model A (2 Predictors) | Model B (19 Predictors) |
|:---|---:|---:|
| R-squared (R²) | 0.5890 | **0.7696** |
| MAE | 1.4690 | **0.4524** |
| MSE | 5.8091 | **3.2560** |
| RMSE | 2.4102 | **1.8044** |

## Model Description

**Model A:** Linear Regression using Attendance and Hours Studied.

**Model B:** Multiple Linear Regression using all 19 independent variables.

## Interpretation

Model B achieved better predictive performance than Model A.

- Higher R-squared indicates better explanatory power.
- Lower MAE indicates smaller average prediction errors.
- Lower MSE indicates lower squared prediction errors.
- Lower RMSE indicates smaller prediction errors in the original target units.

## Conclusion

Model B performed better than Model A across all four evaluation metrics, demonstrating the predictive benefit of including more independent variables in this experiment.
